  "checks": [
    "Exact Proxy/value ownership edges for native Surface and Font; Draw also owns its actual target",
    "All six published XGE functions called directly in generated xlang C",
    "A Draw rejects a foreign backend target and rejects semantic End while value inspection is active",
    "An any-thread native Proxy still creates custom value resources confined to their creator thread",
    "Each resource allocation failed independently under injection; outputs cleared and allocation tracked to baseline",
    "The language exposes state through ordinary and callback views; an independent value survives Font close and Draw finish",
    "The Draw owns its target even after the original language Surface view closes",
    "Expired backend views, ended Draw state reads, and opaque payload from other providers report checked errors",
    "Stock callback resource bridge regression executes with the updated header and binary",
    "Named Proxy registration and eleven existing explicit C descriptor imports coexist in the package"
  ],
  "performanceScope": "XRT allocation events on the same hosted XGE SDK. GCC O2 empty native Surface versus native Surface retaining an already-live value, then JIT xlang construction and read. The output view materialization is included in the xlang counts.",
